 "_README": [
  "THE DESIGN OF RECORD for every rubric desc/rule the graders read.",
  "One sha per (item|slot|field) over whitespace-normalised text.",
  "Seeded 2026-09-06 from the tree as it then stood: the shipped text WAS the",
  "design at that moment, and from here a change to any field must be an",
  "explicit change HERE too.",
  "WHY IT EXISTS: subgoal Q19 designed a slot's desc as prose in a goal entry,",
  "the string was RE-TYPED at build time, the re-typing dropped the question's",
  "comparison clause, every other gate passed, and the sweep cost ~230 calls",
  "measuring a question nobody chose. Every gate asked whether the text was",
  "WELL-FORMED; none asked whether it was THE TEXT SOMEBODY DECIDED ON.",
  "TO CHANGE A FIELD: edit the rubric, then run",
  "  python3 measured.py --accept-design-change ITEM SLOT FIELD",
  "which prints the old and new text and rewrites that ONE sha. There is",
  "deliberately no bulk regenerate: bulk regeneration would make this file",
  "agree with anything and enforce nothing."
 ],
